Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:44:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] replicavault: primary also vaults every delete (F1)

Phase 2 c03: when the retainer is killed while deletes are in flight and its
PGs are then remapped, the deletes it had not yet committed are acknowledged
by the remaining acting set (dup op after the interval change) and the
retainer's unremoved object is later purged with its stray PG copy. 261 of
320 acknowledged deletes were lost.

The primary now vaults every head a transaction deletes, in addition to the
retainer (path=primary; path=fallback when the primary is the retainer).
The ack waits for the primary's commit, and the vault txc is queued ahead of
op_t on the same sequencer, so an acknowledged delete has a durable copy on
the primary whatever happens to the retainer. The recovery path vaults on the
primary as well as on the retainer. Two copies per delete; no message,
peering, PG log, scrub or backfill change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GapZ5dvT4vTJ9FHbVNTeKb
